{title: Jesus Calls Us}
{artist: Cecil F. Alexander / William H. Jude}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 95}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virgnia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 269)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Jesus [D7]calls us over [G]the tumult
[G]Of [C]our life’s wild, rest[B]less, [E7]sea;
[E7]Day [A7]by day [D]His sweet [G]voice soundeth,
[G]Saying, [C]Christian, [D7]follow [G]Me!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]As of [D7]old Saint Andrew [G]heard it
[G]By the [C]Galilean [B]lake,
[E7]Turned from [A7]home and [D]toil and [G]kindred,
[G]Leaving [C]all for [D7]Jesus’ [G]sake.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]In our [D7]joys and in our [G]sorrows,
[G]Days of [C]toil and hours of [B]ease,
[E7]Still He [A7]calls, in [D]cares and [G]pleasures,
[G]Christian, [C]love Me [D7]more than [G]these!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Jesus [D7]calls us! By Thy [G]mercies,
[G]Savior [C]may we hear Thy [B]call,
[E7]Give our [A7]hearts to [D]Thine obe[G]dience,
[G]Serve and [C]love Thee [D7]best of [G]all.
{end_of_verse}
